# Build context for the single-container image only.
#
# Docker prefers <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore over the repo-root .dockerignore,
# so this affects Dockerfile.all-in-one and nothing else. The compose backend
# and frontend builds keep using their own .dockerignore files.
#
# The context was 1.1 GB, nearly all of it data that no stage copies: the
# GlobalML quadkey archives under data/ are 503 MB and old/ is 145 MB. Sending
# that on every build cost minutes for files the build never reads.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/dist
data
old
hmmmm
tests
docs
*.tar.gz
*.md
!backend/**/*.md

# Secrets. These live in .gitignore, but that only governs git: a .env on disk is
# still inside the build context and would be COPY-able into a layer. Runtime
# values are injected with --env-file on the host instead, so nothing here needs
# to ship inside the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
